    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Galleria was introduced in 2007, named after the brand's first boutique, Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II, in Milan's iconic arcade — where Miuccia Prada's grandfather, Mario Prada, launched the house in 1913.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/wtprgy0/bf439f92abb29625.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/wtprgy0/025b13f514c2ec4d.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "Prada Fall 2014 campaign",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/wtprgy0/297f99ddcc5b6f05.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/wtprgy0/c1934dc75403aec7.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The silhouette draws from the frame bags and doctor bags popular in the 1940s, featuring a sleek trapezoidal shape and curved top handles. In Chinese-speaking regions, the Galleria is affectionately known as the 'Killer Bag,' thanks to its appearance in the Mission: Impossible films, where the assassin Sabine Moreau carries it to conceal her pistol.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/wtprgy0/b2c01b8c9a2104c0.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/wtprgy0/b0365f45183ad0b4.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "Mission: Impossible – Ghost Protocol, 2011",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Every hardware detail is meticulously crafted — the most iconic is the central triangular leather badge, designed by founder Mario Prada in 1913 and now a hallmark of the brand. The sides feature snap closures, the handles are adorned with leather tabs and snaps, and four metal feet protect the base from wear.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
